<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply rises to 16.6 pct on June 6.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply rises to 16.6 pct on June 6.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.6 percent on June 6, up from 16.4 percent on May 23, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   June 6, 1997   May 23, 1997  May 24, 1996</p>
<p>		   16.6	     16.4	    16.8</p>
<p>Money supply was 7,258.53 billion rupees on June 6 against 7,199.80 billion rupees on May 23, 1997 and 6,207.91 billion on June 7, 1996, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
